@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Member A - OperationAttempt lifecycle\nMA-0.2 local candidate for C review
hide empty description
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam stateBackgroundColor #EEF4F8
skinparam stateBorderColor #27465B
skinparam ArrowColor #27465B
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF5D9

state PENDING
state EXECUTING
state SUCCEEDED
state FAILED
state UNKNOWN
state RECONCILING
state BLOCKED

PENDING : Bound work; invocation not started
EXECUTING : Invocation reserved or in progress
SUCCEEDED : Confirmed business result saved
FAILED : Confirmed no-effect failure saved
UNKNOWN : Effect unresolved; no query active
RECONCILING : Authorised lookup in progress
BLOCKED : Invocation prevented

[*] --> PENDING : registerWork [real command and approval bound]\n/ Domain.savePending()
PENDING --> EXECUTING : dispatch [G_DISPATCH and claim won]\n/ Domain.reserveAndMarkExecuting()
PENDING --> BLOCKED : dispatchDenied [not invoked]\n/ Domain.saveBlockAndAudit()
EXECUTING --> BLOCKED : preInvokeCheck [guard denied; not invoked]\n/ Domain.saveBlockAndAudit()
EXECUTING --> SUCCEEDED : providerReply [confirmed business success]\n/ Domain.saveResultAndAudit()
EXECUTING --> FAILED : providerReply [confirmed failure; no effect]\n/ Domain.saveFailureAndAudit()
EXECUTING --> UNKNOWN : outcomeUncertain [effect not established]\n/ Domain.saveUnknownAndAudit()

UNKNOWN --> RECONCILING : reconcile [G_LOOKUP and query claim won]\n/ Domain.markReconcilingAndAudit()
RECONCILING --> SUCCEEDED : lookupReply [original effect confirmed]\n/ Domain.saveResultAndAudit()
RECONCILING --> FAILED : lookupReply [confirmed no effect]\n/ Domain.saveFailureAndAudit()
RECONCILING --> UNKNOWN : lookupEnds [inconclusive, unavailable or query orphaned]\n/ Domain.saveUnresolvedAndAudit()
UNKNOWN --> UNKNOWN : recoveryStopped [budget exhausted or lookup unavailable]\n/ Domain.recordManualRecoveryNeed()

SUCCEEDED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]
BLOCKED --> [*]

note left of PENDING
  No real approval: reject and audit;
  do not fabricate an OperationAttempt.
  A losing claimant returns the existing
  receipt without changing the winner.
end note

note right of EXECUTING
  G_DISPATCH: current trusted approval,
  allowed case state, current passing Risk,
  case/input/proposal/review and exact scope,
  expiry, allowlist and provider permission;
  dependencies saved, no prior success or
  unresolved attempt for this logical key.
  At final check, exclude only this worker's
  claimed, not-yet-invoked reservation;
  no other unresolved attempt is allowed.
  Invoke only after durable reservation
  and the final pre-invocation check.
end note

note right of RECONCILING
  G_LOOKUP: authorised access to this
  historical attempt and provider lookup;
  use its saved provider identity and
  fingerprint, without changing approval.
  Approval expiry blocks new effects,
  not authorised discovery of old facts.
  Historical facts do not replace an accepted
  rejection/manual outcome or its case state.
end note

note left of FAILED
  MA-D01: this attempt ends here.
  A retry creates a new operation_id only
  after confirmed no effect, remaining
  budget and all current dispatch guards.
  Under the same approval, retain the
  logical command, provider key and
  fingerprint; preserve the old attempt.
end note

legend bottom
  Candidate assumptions MA-D01 and MA-D02 require C review; details: docs/12.
  MA-D01: one invocation per attempt; FAILED/BLOCKED do not restart this object.
  MA-D02: UNKNOWN has no active query; an inconclusive lookup returns to UNKNOWN.
  MA-Q01: attempt_count meaning remains open; this diagram assigns no increment rule.
  MA-Q02: cross-approval recovery remains open; no automatic new effect or fingerprint reuse.
  State labels retain rc.3 OperationAttempt.status in local rc.4; only SUCCEEDED has an OperationResult payload.
  Domain alone persists local state/results/audit; method labels are internal effects, not new APIs.
  A failed save leaves the last durable state; recovery queries the same attempt before any retry.
  Unknown effects never become terminal merely because recovery stops or the case is handled manually.
  recordManualRecoveryNeed does not reopen or escalate an already accepted rejection/manual outcome.
  Notification events do not change this lifecycle; successful effects are never replayed.
  All attempt records and audit history are retained; a final node does not delete them.
  Trace: AH-10 / UC-04; FR-010/011; NFR-002/004/006/007; BR-003/004.
endlegend
@enduml
